<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The GovTalkDetails/GovTalkErrors block the real XML Gateway test service returned for a
  GetSubmissionStatus poll, sent with a SubmissionNumber and a PresenterID in the order
  GetSubmissionStatus-v2-9.xsd's content model requires: ((CompanyNumber|SubmissionNumber),
  PresenterID). Observed against ci-claud0efc, polling submission number 000004 (presenter
  E0000052288, company 06846849), twice within five minutes of the submission's own
  acknowledgement, 2026-09-13: identical both times.

  Like Accounts_reject_response_GovTalkErrors.xml, this is not a byte-for-byte capture of the
  full response envelope: the Lambda logs the HTTP status of the gateway call but not the
  response body, so only the fields below - taken from parseGatewayResponse()'s output, which
  the Lambda did return to the caller - are real gateway values. The surrounding envelope
  (Header, Qualifier) was not captured.
-->
<GovTalkErrors>
  <Error>
    <RaisedBy>GetSubmissionStatus</RaisedBy>
    <Number>9999</Number>
    <Type>fatal</Type>
    <Text>No presenter ID supplied</Text>
    <Location></Location>
  </Error>
</GovTalkErrors>
